= Genetics — Technical =

Genetic analysis connects inherited variants to transmission and phenotype using molecular, statistical, and population models. Depending on the question, inference may involve segregation ratios, recombination, penetrance, quantitative-genetic variance components, association, or causal experiments.

== Modeling / evidence cautions ==
* genetics ≠ genomics
* gene influence ≠ single-gene determinism
* heritability ≠ immutability

